@@ -0,0 +1,61 @@
+# OpenCode OS on Windows 10/11
+
+## Just want the app?
+
+Grab the installer from **GitHub → Actions → "Windows Installer"** (or a Release for a `v*` tag):
+`OpenCode OS_0.1.0_x64-setup.exe` (per-user NSIS, no admin needed) or the `.msi`.
+On first launch the setup wizard installs the OpenCode CLI and links your free
+[Zen key](https://opencode.ai/auth).
+
+## Build it yourself (PowerShell)
+
+1. **Node.js 22+** — `winget install OpenJS.NodeJS.LTS`
+2. **Rust** — `winget install Rustlang.Rustup`, then `rustup default stable-msvc`
+3. **MSVC Build Tools** — `winget install Microsoft.VisualStudio.2022.BuildTools --override "--quiet --add Microsoft.VisualStudio.Workload.VCTools --includeRecommended"`
+4. **WebView2** — already present on Windows 10 (recent) and 11; otherwise https://developer.microsoft.com/microsoft-edge/webview2/
+
+Open a **new** PowerShell after installing so PATH is refreshed, then:
+
+```powershell
+npm ci
+npm run tauri:dev      # native window, hot reload of ui/
+npm run tauri:build    # installers -> src-tauri\target\release\bundle\{nsis,msi}\
+npm start              # browser mode at http://127.0.0.1:8787 (no Rust needed)
+npm test               # unit + bridge tests
+npm run test:rust      # opencode-core tests
+```
+
+## OpenCode CLI
+
+The wizard runs `irm https://opencode.ai/install.ps1 | iex` for you. To do it by hand:
+run that line in PowerShell, or `npm i -g opencode-ai` (creates an `opencode.cmd` shim —
+the desktop app handles that; browser mode `npm start` needs a native `opencode.exe`,
+or set `OPENCODE_BIN` to it).
+
+Check your key: 
+
+```powershell
+$env:OPENCODE_API_KEY = "sk-..."
+npm run zen:check
+```
+
+## Where things live
+
+| What | Windows path |
+|------|--------------|
+| Settings + API key | `%APPDATA%\opencode-os\settings.json` |
+| Default workspace | `%USERPROFILE%\OpenCodeWorkspace` |
+| Trash | `<workspace>\.Trash` |
+
+## What changed vs the Linux setup
+
+- Sandbox check now canonicalises the workspace (Windows returns `\\?\C:\…` paths, which broke the
+  `starts_with` test — every file operation would have been rejected).
+- CLI is launched without flashing a console window; `opencode.cmd` shims are found; PATH is
+  reloaded after the installer runs, so no app restart is needed.
+- `zen-check.sh` → cross-platform `scripts/zen-check.mjs`; `gen:icons` points at the real script.
+- Tests no longer depend on a shebang + `:`-separated PATH (`OPENCODE_BIN` / `OPENCODE_BIN_PREFIX`).
+- `npm test` lists files explicitly (`node --test tests` fails on Node 22, and cmd.exe doesn't expand globs).
+- The Rust symlink test is `#[cfg(unix)]`; the settings test no longer writes to your real `%APPDATA%`.
+- `npm run e2e` / `gates:verify` e2e layer needs POSIX shell quoting: run in WSL or CI
+  (skipped on native Windows unless `FORCE_E2E=1`).
